source_cleanup:
  status: completed_and_published_in_1.1.1
  removed: Obsolete pre-SLM2 Rust CLI, v0 fixtures, tracked single-file model demo, and stale duplicate-checkout path dependency.
  authority: Deleted material remains only in Git history and has no executable, compatibility, fallback, or test authority.
  current_implementation: Strict metadata-only SLM2 catalog, peer-feed validator, and browser surface.
  native_companion: Current implementation belongs to the canonical TinyRustLM.com dotnet projects and Rust crates; this historical removal does not instruct agents to rebuild that owner or assert a deployed native release.

memory_endpoints_authority:
  uses: 2
  direct_agent_lane: Agents working across every maintained ecosystem site use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  user_plugin_lane: A TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects the MemoryEndpoints.com plugin as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  separation: Lane identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts remain separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  resilient_prelaunch_duplication: During prelaunch, long-term memory may also be duplicated in .uai files, wikis, public-safe notes, and approved private stores for resilience. Every maintained copy must remain current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  evidence_boundary: Authorization, source, configuration, or reachability alone is not proof of a live MemoryEndpoints meeting, user round, or continuity receipt.

clean_slate_rules:
  - One current SLM2 catalog and acquisition contract only.
  - No legacy reader, compatibility alias, migration, repair, remote inference fallback, hidden retry, best-of-N, or accepted debt.
  - Failed and obsolete receipts remain historical evidence and never become current acceptance logic.

